<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="SweetSue-G-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1928
Composer:	Victor Young
Lyricist:	Will J. Harris
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Swing
Key:	G major

“Sweet Sue, Just You” was published in 1928 and
became a popular song and jazz standard, recorded
by artists including Ben Pollack, Django Reinhardt,
and Benny Goodman. Its exact first performance is
uncertain; early recordings appeared around the time
of publication.</spComments>
